Ragged Roost is an abandoned mining town a little under a day's drive out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], barely on modern maps. Its mine was small, and once ore could be shipped in from the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Infinite Horizon]] for less than it cost to dig here, there was no reason to keep working it, so the Orgs took what was worth packing and left the rest. A rusted sign at the town line reads "Welcome to Ragged Roost, population" with the number scribbled out to zero. A main street runs through the town with a few streets branching off it, one and two story buildings, and above the town on the mountainside sits the old rock crusher and its conveyor, unused.

The [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] the Party holds an invitation to is held here. On the night of the gathering the old oil street lamps have been given electricity and hung with fairy lights, banners reading "Pilgrimage Welcome" hang from them, and tables of hors d'oeuvres and champagne are set out along the main street. Hundreds of guests walk the street in elegant dress and masks, animal masks and plain ones and ornate masquerade masks, some of them with three or four armed attendants. Spotlights throw light up into the sky, bright enough to be seen ten miles off, and signs direct cars to a parking lot at the edge of town, where a line of guests waits at a table to have their invitations checked and to be handed masks.

The centerpiece of the gathering stands at the middle of town: an Istrian strider under construction, scaffolding all around it, a platform carried on eight legs with buildings set on top, three or four stories up and the size of a cruise ship. It was unfinished when the Party arrived.

Crossing the town line brings a pins-and-needles feeling at the small of the back, and every raiment within the town turns a plain matte gray, all of them the same color, shape and size and half-transparent, so that no guest can be read for their god. The blessings themselves still work. [[Aut]]'s mark still showed on [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] when he called it up, and still answered him.

The gathering was held on the night of the Party's arrival. Its host stood on the strider's scaffolding and announced a hunt for the twenty [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystones]], and named the strider the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. Beyond the main street, a path marked with crossed swords led to a disused train yard where Harlequins ran a trial by combat, and one marked with a fairy ring led off toward the town's outskirts.
